WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.760
- Now, when Tucker Carlson said

00:00:01.760 --> 00:00:03.490
that we should be calling the police

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:05.020
or child protective services

00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:07.050
anytime a child is wearing a mask

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:09.350
because that parent is
committing child abuse,

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:10.530
something struck me.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.770
And no, it wasn't exactly
the complete lunacy

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.420
and insanity of the statement

00:00:15.420 --> 00:00:18.240
that was clearly just
designed to trigger the libs,

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:21.200
and to get people to rage
watch Tucker Carlson,

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:22.930
it was that there was a decent chance

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:24.640
that Tucker Carlson was asking people

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.000
to commit an actual crime

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:30.478
in the name of this stupid
mask-related culture war.

00:00:30.478 --> 00:00:32.420
(bright music)

00:00:32.420 --> 00:00:34.440
- [Advertiser] Sponsored by
CuriosityStream and Nebula.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.360
- Hey, legal eagles, it's
time to think like a lawyer,

00:00:36.360 --> 00:00:38.850
because if you do what
Tucker Carlson says,

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.430
well, there's a decent
chance you might go to jail.

00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:43.910
If you haven't been following along,

00:00:43.910 --> 00:00:46.970
Tucker Carlson, the ostensible
hater of big government

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:48.550
and champion on personal freedom,

00:00:48.550 --> 00:00:50.530
has suddenly found a darn good reason

00:00:50.530 --> 00:00:52.380
why the big government should interfere

00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:53.490
with your personal freedom,

00:00:53.490 --> 00:00:56.810
specifically your right
to raise your children

00:00:56.810 --> 00:00:58.550
the way that you want to.

00:00:58.550 --> 00:01:01.780
Remember, this is the
party of family values.

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:03.510
So, what is this emergency

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.100
that justifies swift governmental action?

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.020
Human trafficking?

00:01:07.020 --> 00:01:08.270
Terrorism?

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:09.103
Well, no.

00:01:09.103 --> 00:01:11.420
It's actually something
much more sinister.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.253
It's

00:01:12.253 --> 00:01:14.693
children wearing cloth masks.

00:01:14.693 --> 00:01:18.260
(suspenseful music)

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.550
- So, next time you see someone
in a mask on the sidewalk

00:01:20.550 --> 00:01:22.580
or on the bike path, do not hesitate.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:24.067
Ask politely, but firmly.

00:01:24.067 --> 00:01:26.190
"Would you please take off your mask?

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.890
Science shows there is no
reason for you to be wearing it.

00:01:28.890 --> 00:01:31.330
Your mask is making me uncomfortable."

00:01:31.330 --> 00:01:32.940
- Oh yes, the libertarian wants people

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:35.220
to stop doing something that
doesn't affect other people

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:36.980
in any way whatsoever.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:38.620
- Masks are for the guilty.

00:01:38.620 --> 00:01:40.780
They're signifiers of
shame and submission.

00:01:40.780 --> 00:01:42.180
- And guy who ostensibly says

00:01:42.180 --> 00:01:44.590
that he wants the government
to leave him alone

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:46.740
included a rant that
recommended that his viewers

00:01:46.740 --> 00:01:49.220
call the cops if they see a child outside

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:50.220
wearing a mask.

00:01:50.220 --> 00:01:51.850
- Call the police immediately.

00:01:51.850 --> 00:01:53.810
Contact child protective services.

00:01:53.810 --> 00:01:55.360
Keep calling until someone arrives.

00:01:55.360 --> 00:01:57.050
- Yes. Apparently, parents everywhere

00:01:57.050 --> 00:01:59.050
are committing mass child abuse,

00:01:59.050 --> 00:02:00.580
like these people

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:02.050
and these people

00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:03.400
and these people.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.300
Yes, these people are all
monsters committing child abuse

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.040
and they must be stopped

00:02:08.040 --> 00:02:09.040
because here's the thing,

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:10.530
putting aside the legal repercussions

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:12.910
of calling the CPS or the police,

00:02:12.910 --> 00:02:14.890
which we'll get to in just a second,

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:17.400
as we've seen time and
time again in the news,

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.530
anytime the police are
called for anything,

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:23.480
it has the possibility of
turning violent if not lethal.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:25.790
For better or worse, the police are armed.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:30.430
And any law, whether it is
passing off a fake $20 bill

00:02:30.430 --> 00:02:31.780
or trying to sell cigarettes

00:02:31.780 --> 00:02:34.010
without the correct certificate,

00:02:34.010 --> 00:02:36.260
has the possibility of being enforced

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:37.920
at the barrel of a gun.

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:40.260
And of course, the real
civil libertarians,

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:41.510
not Tucker Carlson,

00:02:41.510 --> 00:02:43.830
have recognized that the
preponderance of laws

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.210
in this country,

00:02:45.210 --> 00:02:46.860
it may not happen very often,

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:49.800
but have the possibility of being enforced

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:53.000
by people with guns and
things can turn south.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:56.160
Do not call the police unnecessarily.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:02:59.240
So, the point that I think
Tucker is trying to make here

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.520
is that he doesn't
agree with mask mandates

00:03:01.520 --> 00:03:04.600
that require people and
children to wear masks outdoors

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:06.720
because outdoor transmission is low,

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:10.880
and the added benefit from
wearing a mask is negligible

00:03:10.880 --> 00:03:13.160
because the transmission of COVID outdoors

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:14.280
is just low to begin with.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:17.120
And fine, that's very probably true,

00:03:17.120 --> 00:03:20.740
but when people are being
faced with a global pandemic

00:03:20.740 --> 00:03:23.490
where now over 500,000
Americans have died,

00:03:23.490 --> 00:03:25.880
it's probably okay for people
to freak out a little bit.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.240
And it's a false equivalency to say that

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.900
even if there were no outdoor
transmission whatsoever,

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:32.400
that there's no reason for a mask mandate.

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.540
It's not the same thing to say

00:03:33.540 --> 00:03:35.930
that the only reason for
an outdoor mask mandate

00:03:35.930 --> 00:03:37.760
might be to prevent outdoor transmission.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.840
For example, maybe wearing a mask outdoors

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:41.960
makes it more likely that
you'll wear one indoors.

00:03:41.960 --> 00:03:45.130
Maybe it guarantees that you'll
have a mask on your person

00:03:45.130 --> 00:03:47.210
when you decide to walk indoors.

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:49.860
Maybe it normalizes the idea
of wearing masks in general.

00:03:49.860 --> 00:03:51.500
After all, these are the same people

00:03:51.500 --> 00:03:54.800
that made wearing a mask
full stop, a cultural issue.

00:03:54.800 --> 00:03:57.350
And of course, when we
talk about laws like these,

00:03:57.350 --> 00:03:59.120
they undergo rational basis reviews.

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:03.760
So, as long as there is some
rational reason for these laws

00:04:03.760 --> 00:04:06.370
that makes the laws constitutional.

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.170
And there were probably
lots of other reasons

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:10.780
apart from stopping outdoor transmission.

00:04:10.780 --> 00:04:11.830
And I think even at this point,

00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:14.490
Tucker isn't arguing against
wearing masks indoors

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.130
until everyone is vaccinated.

00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:18.020
And then, there is another logical fallacy

00:04:18.020 --> 00:04:19.120
of false equivalency

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:20.510
where Tucker is conflating the idea

00:04:20.510 --> 00:04:22.810
that even if there's no
reason to wear a mask outdoors

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.670
that it being actual child abuse

00:04:24.670 --> 00:04:27.690
to make children wear masks outdoors.

00:04:27.690 --> 00:04:28.760
That is not the case.

00:04:28.760 --> 00:04:30.450
We'll talk about that
more in just a second.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.800
And sure, some of this reads as

00:04:32.800 --> 00:04:34.830
giving people their own medicine,

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:36.190
to the extent that he's saying that people

00:04:36.190 --> 00:04:38.620
who are freaked out about
a deadly global pandemic

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:42.170
and they understandably wanted
other people to wear masks

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.110
but the risks were always asymmetric,

00:04:44.110 --> 00:04:46.500
not wearing a mask endangered other people

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:50.420
in a way that wearing a mask
simply doesn't and never did.

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:52.300
But look, it's possible that he is simply

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:54.870
satirically saying that
people should call the cops

00:04:54.870 --> 00:04:56.160
and child protective services

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:58.560
when they see children
outdoors wearing masks.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:00.600
Honestly, I can't tell at this point.

00:05:00.600 --> 00:05:02.430
I don't even know if
Tucker Carlson himself

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:03.990
is satire or not,

00:05:03.990 --> 00:05:07.220
and I can't tell if his
recommendation is satirical.

00:05:07.220 --> 00:05:09.410
But honestly, it sounds genuine enough

00:05:09.410 --> 00:05:10.490
to at least talk about

00:05:10.490 --> 00:05:13.230
whether this recommendation
is illegal or not.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:15.890
So, either way let's have
some fun with this idiocy.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:18.220
But let's delve into what would happen

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.310
if one of Tucker Carlson's viewers

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:22.100
actually called child protective services

00:05:22.100 --> 00:05:26.050
or the cops on parenting for
putting masks on children.

00:05:26.050 --> 00:05:26.883
Now, generally speaking,

00:05:26.883 --> 00:05:28.070
in America, parents have the right

00:05:28.070 --> 00:05:29.970
to decide matters involving
their children's health,

00:05:29.970 --> 00:05:31.090
welfare, and education.

00:05:31.090 --> 00:05:32.730
Although the state will step in

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.563
when there is abuse,
neglect, or mistreatment,

00:05:34.563 --> 00:05:36.320
parents have the right to decide

00:05:36.320 --> 00:05:38.420
what their children listen
to, where they go to church,

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:40.210
where they go to school, what they wear,

00:05:40.210 --> 00:05:42.280
and the medical care that they receive.

00:05:42.280 --> 00:05:45.150
And Tucker Carlson is
on board with us mostly.

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.300
He believes it is
authoritarian for the state

00:05:47.300 --> 00:05:49.070
to require children to be vaccinated

00:05:49.070 --> 00:05:51.290
but not authoritarian for the state

00:05:51.290 --> 00:05:54.060
to investigate parents whose
children appear in public

00:05:54.060 --> 00:05:55.330
with masks.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:58.190
Now, Tucker is correct that
states are empowered to

00:05:58.190 --> 00:06:00.480
investigate reports of abuse and neglect.

00:06:00.480 --> 00:06:03.680
Society is rightfully concerned
about children's welfare

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.120
and federal and state laws
require some professionals

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.290
who actually mandatorily
report if they suspect abuse.

00:06:09.290 --> 00:06:11.530
These are known as mandatory reporters

00:06:11.530 --> 00:06:14.320
and they include people like
doctors, social workers,

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:15.230
and teachers.

00:06:15.230 --> 00:06:16.490
And since we're talking
about the substance

00:06:16.490 --> 00:06:17.950
of these reports,

00:06:17.950 --> 00:06:19.620
let's address the elephant in the room.

00:06:19.620 --> 00:06:21.910
No, making your children wear masks

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:23.420
is not child abuse,

00:06:23.420 --> 00:06:26.970
no more so than making your
child wear a hat or a sweater.

00:06:26.970 --> 00:06:29.500
And look, given the number
of scratchy wool sweaters

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:31.290
that my parents made me
wear when I was young,

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.710
I can understand why people
wouldn't wanna do it,

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:37.180
but it doesn't rise to
the level of child abuse.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.020
So, I feel extremely
confident in saying that

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:42.940
making your children wear masks
outdoors is not child abuse.

00:06:42.940 --> 00:06:45.180
Parents can force their
kids to do a lot of things

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:47.160
that have no scientific basis,

00:06:47.160 --> 00:06:49.340
making them do things is not child abuse.

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:52.420
For example, if a child doesn't
wanna go trick or treating,

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:54.830
a parent could force them
to go trick or treating,

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:56.420
and gasp

00:06:56.420 --> 00:06:57.590
wear a mask.

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.590
That's not child abuse.

00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:02.530
Parents don't need a
genuine scientific basis

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:05.130
for everything that
they make their kids do.

00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:07.440
Parents can force their kids
to wash behind their ears

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:08.830
with no scientific basis,

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:09.800
whether that's helpful or not.

00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.830
They can force kids to eat carrots

00:07:11.830 --> 00:07:13.260
even though there's no scientific basis

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:14.390
that it will help their eyesight.

00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:15.730
And they can tell kids

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:17.270
to turn off the dome light in the car

00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.120
even though it's definitively not illegal

00:07:19.120 --> 00:07:21.010
as I proved in my other video.

00:07:21.010 --> 00:07:22.710
Kids don't like doing lots of things

00:07:22.710 --> 00:07:23.690
that they're forced to do,

00:07:23.690 --> 00:07:25.660
often because kids are really dumb.

00:07:25.660 --> 00:07:27.790
And parents are not committing child abuse

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:29.460
just because they're
making kids do something

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:30.293
that they might not have

00:07:30.293 --> 00:07:32.870
all of the scientific rationale for.

00:07:32.870 --> 00:07:35.530
And the same is obviously
true for masks as well.

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:36.550
If you think that masks

00:07:36.550 --> 00:07:38.810
appreciably change your oxygen levels,

00:07:38.810 --> 00:07:41.020
or have some other deleterious effects,

00:07:41.020 --> 00:07:43.000
may I recommend the channel Medlife Crisis

00:07:43.000 --> 00:07:45.210
run by my friend, Dr. Rohin Francis,

00:07:45.210 --> 00:07:48.830
or the Doctor Mike
channel run by Dr. Mike,

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.670
who will disabuse you of the notion

00:07:50.670 --> 00:07:54.480
that wearing a mask could
possibly lead to child abuse.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:56.000
But, you already knew that.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:58.610
Though on the other hand,
scratchy wool sweaters,

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:01.690
that's going to have to be
the subject for another video.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:04.650
But, let's talk about mandatory reporting.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:06.480
In 1974, the U.S. enacted

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:08.470
the Child Abuse Prevention
and Treatment Act

00:08:08.470 --> 00:08:11.170
which requires all states to
add provisions to their laws

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:14.210
that protect mandatory
reporters from legal retaliation

00:08:14.210 --> 00:08:15.800
for making a report.

00:08:15.800 --> 00:08:17.930
This legal protection is called immunity.

00:08:17.930 --> 00:08:20.790
And without immunity, a
mandatory reporter could be sued

00:08:20.790 --> 00:08:24.400
if the report was not substantiated
after the investigation.

00:08:24.400 --> 00:08:26.170
The law recognizes that
in some situations,

00:08:26.170 --> 00:08:28.060
the mandatory reporter might not be sure

00:08:28.060 --> 00:08:29.990
about whether a child is
being abused or neglected.

00:08:29.990 --> 00:08:31.690
Therefore, in most jurisdictions,

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:34.100
mandatory reporters are
protected by immunity

00:08:34.100 --> 00:08:36.910
as long as the report
was made in good faith.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:39.790
If that's true, they can't
be sued or prosecuted.

00:08:39.790 --> 00:08:42.090
And at least 15 States in
the District of Columbia,

00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.100
the presumption of good
faith applies to everyone,

00:08:44.100 --> 00:08:45.480
not just mandatory reporters.

00:08:45.480 --> 00:08:47.850
So, if Joe Schmo watched Tucker Carlson

00:08:47.850 --> 00:08:49.170
and got the idea to call CPS

00:08:49.170 --> 00:08:51.512
because his neighbor's child was outside,

00:08:51.512 --> 00:08:53.430
Oh, no wearing a mask,

00:08:53.430 --> 00:08:54.530
there would be a presumption

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:56.630
that the person acted in good faith,

00:08:56.630 --> 00:09:00.090
but that's only in 15 States
and that's only a presumption.

00:09:00.090 --> 00:09:01.240
An aggrieved parent

00:09:01.240 --> 00:09:03.230
might be able to overcome
that presumption.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.420
The unfortunate reality is that

00:09:04.420 --> 00:09:07.500
sometimes people do make false
reports of abuse and neglect.

00:09:07.500 --> 00:09:09.250
And that's why there are
laws making it illegal

00:09:09.250 --> 00:09:11.950
to file false reports of
child abuse, mistreatment,

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:13.040
or neglect.

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:14.370
The logic behind these laws is that

00:09:14.370 --> 00:09:16.070
anytime a false report comes in,

00:09:16.070 --> 00:09:17.570
it distracts from the time and resources

00:09:17.570 --> 00:09:18.670
investigators could have

00:09:18.670 --> 00:09:21.530
to pursue real cases of
child abuse and neglect.

00:09:21.530 --> 00:09:23.950
And at least 29 states in Puerto Rico

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:26.570
penalize any person who
willfully or intentionally

00:09:26.570 --> 00:09:29.600
makes a false report of
child abuse or neglect.

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.640
19 States in the Virgin Islands
classify false reporting

00:09:32.640 --> 00:09:34.630
as a misdemeanor or similar charge.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.080
In Florida, Illinois,
Tennessee, and Texas,

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:39.810
making a false report of
abuse or neglect is a felony.

00:09:39.810 --> 00:09:40.850
And in other States,

00:09:40.850 --> 00:09:43.180
subsequent offenses are
upgraded to felonies.

00:09:43.180 --> 00:09:45.800
Now, California, Maine,
Minnesota, Montana, and Nebraska

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:48.260
don't impose criminal
penalties for false reports.

00:09:48.260 --> 00:09:49.790
Instead, they strip legal immunity

00:09:49.790 --> 00:09:51.600
from people who make false claims.

00:09:51.600 --> 00:09:54.010
This means that individuals
could face criminal penalties

00:09:54.010 --> 00:09:56.320
for filing false police
reports, perjuring themselves,

00:09:56.320 --> 00:09:58.980
or being sued for damages.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:01.370
And that means the Karen's
and Tucker's of the world

00:10:01.370 --> 00:10:03.330
who make false CPS reports

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.120
could face some serious sanctions.

00:10:05.120 --> 00:10:07.170
So, what would qualify as a false report?

00:10:07.170 --> 00:10:10.270
And is that what Tucker is
asking his audience to do?

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:12.420
Well, an unfounded or
unsubstantiated report

00:10:12.420 --> 00:10:14.750
is not the same thing as a false report.

00:10:14.750 --> 00:10:17.640
So, would the scenario that
Tucker Carlson outlined

00:10:17.640 --> 00:10:20.000
actually be considered a
false report under the law?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:21.660
Well, generally the legal
standard for determining

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:22.950
whether the report is actually false

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:24.930
is knowingly and willfully.

00:10:24.930 --> 00:10:26.770
This definition comes
from Pennsylvania Law

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:27.920
and is fairly common.

00:10:27.920 --> 00:10:28.753
This generally means

00:10:28.753 --> 00:10:30.870
that the person must
be acting in bad faith.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:32.600
They must they've known
or knew it was likely

00:10:32.600 --> 00:10:34.200
that the report was false.

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:35.910
Erik Wemple of The Washington Post

00:10:35.910 --> 00:10:38.280
contacted child service
departments in several states

00:10:38.280 --> 00:10:40.480
and asked whether the
states could investigate

00:10:40.480 --> 00:10:42.870
a Tucker report for abuse and neglect.

00:10:42.870 --> 00:10:44.790
Minnesota said wearing a mask or not

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:47.490
does not rise to the
level of abuse or neglect.

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:50.270
New Jersey said that the wearing
or not wearing of a mask,

00:10:50.270 --> 00:10:51.760
whether inside or outside,

00:10:51.760 --> 00:10:53.720
is not by itself considered abusive.

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:55.290
And Nevada had a forceful statement

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:56.600
explaining why this kind of call

00:10:56.600 --> 00:10:58.077
could do actual damage.

00:10:58.077 --> 00:11:00.670
"In no circumstance would a
child wearing a mask in public

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:02.880
to reduce or prevent the spread of disease

00:11:02.880 --> 00:11:05.380
meet Nevada's definition of
abuse or neglect of a child

00:11:05.380 --> 00:11:06.930
pursuant to NRS 432B.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:10.460
The State's child welfare
agencies have limited resources

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:12.700
to address real issues
of abuse and neglect

00:11:12.700 --> 00:11:15.480
and if Nevada does see a
surge of nonsense calls,

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:17.580
children in threat of actual harm

00:11:17.580 --> 00:11:19.580
will be in increased danger."

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.740
And that's just to child
protective services.

00:11:21.740 --> 00:11:24.530
Filing a false police report
is an example of speech

00:11:24.530 --> 00:11:26.620
that is not protected
by the first amendment.

00:11:26.620 --> 00:11:28.020
To prove that a person
committed this crime,

00:11:28.020 --> 00:11:29.720
the prosecutor generally has to show first

00:11:29.720 --> 00:11:31.330
that the defendant filed a report

00:11:31.330 --> 00:11:33.360
with an investigative agency
like a police department

00:11:33.360 --> 00:11:36.070
or local district attorney,
state attorney general or CPS.

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.220
And second, that the defendant
knew or had reason to believe

00:11:39.220 --> 00:11:40.870
that the report was false.

00:11:40.870 --> 00:11:41.703
In some jurisdictions,

00:11:41.703 --> 00:11:43.140
the prosecutor must also prove

00:11:43.140 --> 00:11:44.890
that the defendant made
the false statement

00:11:44.890 --> 00:11:46.120
with the intent to interfere

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:47.390
with the criminal justice system.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:48.480
In Virginia for instance,

00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:49.850
the prosecutor has to show that the caller

00:11:49.850 --> 00:11:51.410
intended to mislead or interfere

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:53.810
with the operation of a
law enforcement agency.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:55.560
And on top of that,
some states have passed

00:11:55.560 --> 00:11:58.870
so-called anti-Karen
laws to address the raft

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:01.260
of spurious 911 calls that have been made.

00:12:01.260 --> 00:12:03.740
For example, after a new
Yorker named Amy Cooper

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:06.080
called 911 to report a black
man was threatening her

00:12:06.080 --> 00:12:09.370
because he asked her to leash
her dog in Central Park.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:10.410
The mean became a movement

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:13.210
to hold people accountable
for making false 911 calls.

00:12:13.210 --> 00:12:15.480
Now, some cities and
states are passing laws

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:17.830
to stop these Karens from
wasting everyone's time,

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:19.180
and after the Cooper incident,

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:20.370
Virginia was one of the states

00:12:20.370 --> 00:12:22.600
who added anti-Karen legislation.

00:12:22.600 --> 00:12:24.830
The Virginia code prohibiting
false police reports

00:12:24.830 --> 00:12:28.190
was amended to make filing a
false report a Class 6 felony

00:12:28.190 --> 00:12:30.597
if the report was motivated
by discrimination.

00:12:30.597 --> 00:12:32.770
"If a person intentionally
gives a false report

00:12:32.770 --> 00:12:34.210
as to the commission of any crime

00:12:34.210 --> 00:12:35.870
to any law-enforcement official,

00:12:35.870 --> 00:12:37.560
causes another to give a false report

00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:38.760
to any law-enforcement official,

00:12:38.760 --> 00:12:41.330
or calls or summons any
law-enforcement official

00:12:41.330 --> 00:12:42.430
against another person

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:44.650
because of his race,
religious conviction, gender,

00:12:44.650 --> 00:12:46.970
disability, gender identity,
sexual orientation,

00:12:46.970 --> 00:12:48.500
color, or national origin,

00:12:48.500 --> 00:12:50.530
the person is guilty of a Class 6 felony."

00:12:50.530 --> 00:12:52.570
In addition to new harsher
criminal penalties,

00:12:52.570 --> 00:12:54.450
cities like San Francisco
have approved legislation

00:12:54.450 --> 00:12:56.500
to give people who were targets of a Karen

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.010
the right to sue the caller.

00:12:58.010 --> 00:13:00.200
And this of course makes Tucker Carlson

00:13:00.200 --> 00:13:02.320
the biggest Karen of them all.

00:13:02.320 --> 00:13:04.020
- Call the police immediately.

00:13:04.020 --> 00:13:05.520
- Though, in fairness to Tucker Carlson,

00:13:05.520 --> 00:13:08.170
at least in this particular instance,

00:13:08.170 --> 00:13:11.220
these calls don't seem to be
motivated by discrimination,

00:13:11.220 --> 00:13:14.890
rather just an incredibly
misguided right wing culture war.

00:13:14.890 --> 00:13:17.330
And these are just the
statutory criminal issues.

00:13:17.330 --> 00:13:19.640
A criminal issue needs to
be brought by the state,

00:13:19.640 --> 00:13:21.580
the district attorney usually.

00:13:21.580 --> 00:13:23.010
Then, there's also the possibility

00:13:23.010 --> 00:13:25.570
that a victim of these reports

00:13:25.570 --> 00:13:28.530
could just simply sue the
person for civil damages

00:13:28.530 --> 00:13:30.190
related to the actions.

00:13:30.190 --> 00:13:32.850
And a parent could bring a
lawsuit for something called

00:13:32.850 --> 00:13:34.980
intentional infliction
of emotional distress

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:37.313
against a person who makes a false report.

00:13:37.313 --> 00:13:40.530
IIED is a tort claim that
focuses on intentional conduct

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:42.530
resulting in extreme emotional distress

00:13:42.530 --> 00:13:43.920
which causes a mental reaction

00:13:43.920 --> 00:13:46.100
such as anguish, grief, or fright.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:47.400
To prove a claim for IIED,

00:13:47.400 --> 00:13:49.470
a plaintiff has to
establish four elements.

00:13:49.470 --> 00:13:52.000
One, that the defendant acted
intentionally and recklessly,

00:13:52.000 --> 00:13:54.600
the defendant's conduct
was extreme and outrageous,

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:57.280
the defendant's act is
the cause of the distress,

00:13:57.280 --> 00:14:00.180
and the plaintiff suffered
severe emotional distress

00:14:00.180 --> 00:14:02.380
as a result of the defendant's conduct.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:03.213
Though, in fairness,

00:14:03.213 --> 00:14:05.870
it can be incredibly difficult
to make an IIED claim.

00:14:05.870 --> 00:14:07.930
Some legal commentators
go so far as to call this

00:14:07.930 --> 00:14:10.600
the civil equivalent of a RICO prosecution

00:14:10.600 --> 00:14:12.830
because it's just never RICO.

00:14:12.830 --> 00:14:14.450
But it's difficult for
a plaintiff to prove

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.620
that conduct was so extreme or outrageous

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:18.360
that it caused severe anguish

00:14:18.360 --> 00:14:20.730
resulting in recoverable damages.

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:22.350
Though a plaintiff would probably say

00:14:22.350 --> 00:14:24.820
that this is the equivalent
of getting swatted

00:14:24.820 --> 00:14:29.560
where there's the real
possibility of injury or death,

00:14:29.560 --> 00:14:32.190
and no one likes having the police called

00:14:32.190 --> 00:14:36.000
for something as ridiculous
as wearing a mask.

00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.610
So under some circumstances,

00:14:37.610 --> 00:14:40.530
someone might be able to
make a civil case for IIED

00:14:40.530 --> 00:14:42.250
related to one of these calls.

00:14:42.250 --> 00:14:44.290
But if you tried to make
a case against someone

00:14:44.290 --> 00:14:45.630
making a Tucker report,

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:47.100
it's not going to be a slam dunk

00:14:47.100 --> 00:14:49.530
because there's going to
be many defenses available.

00:14:49.530 --> 00:14:50.670
The first of which is that

00:14:50.670 --> 00:14:52.990
there's a difference between
making up a complete lie

00:14:52.990 --> 00:14:55.710
about something that
never factually happened

00:14:55.710 --> 00:14:57.890
and calling child protective services

00:14:57.890 --> 00:15:00.530
because of something
that did actually happen

00:15:00.530 --> 00:15:03.570
that you mistakenly believe gives rise

00:15:03.570 --> 00:15:05.560
to something called child abuse.

00:15:05.560 --> 00:15:07.660
And so, the main defense
to any of these charges

00:15:07.660 --> 00:15:09.900
would be that the person
who reported the masks

00:15:09.900 --> 00:15:10.780
had a good faith belief

00:15:10.780 --> 00:15:13.200
that they were witnessing
something that was concerning.

00:15:13.200 --> 00:15:14.320
After all,

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:17.930
they saw it on TV that if
a child is wearing a mask,

00:15:17.930 --> 00:15:20.120
it must be child abuse.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:21.810
That's the thing about good faith beliefs,

00:15:21.810 --> 00:15:25.080
is that the person might
be a complete nutcase

00:15:25.080 --> 00:15:27.610
but if they subjectively
believe that to be the case,

00:15:27.610 --> 00:15:29.620
they might be operating in good faith.

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.890
If they said they feared
the child couldn't breathe,

00:15:31.890 --> 00:15:33.580
or was having an asthma attack,

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:35.410
or had faxed to back up their assertion

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:37.300
that the child's health was compromised,

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:39.190
maybe the report could be legitimate.

00:15:39.190 --> 00:15:41.420
And it would be incredibly
difficult for someone to prove

00:15:41.420 --> 00:15:43.800
that the person who was
making the Tucker report

00:15:43.800 --> 00:15:45.900
was doing it out of spite or doing it

00:15:45.900 --> 00:15:49.210
to intentionally harm the
parents of the children

00:15:49.210 --> 00:15:50.660
that were wearing masks.

00:15:50.660 --> 00:15:51.493
But on the other hand,

00:15:51.493 --> 00:15:54.270
Tucker's making such
a facially ridiculous,

00:15:54.270 --> 00:15:56.070
objectively unreasonable argument,

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:58.190
that maybe it's not possible for someone

00:15:58.190 --> 00:16:00.330
to have an actual good
faith of subjective belief

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:02.000
under these circumstances.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.970
Clearly, wearing a mask doesn't rise

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:05.990
to the level of child abuse,

00:16:05.990 --> 00:16:08.890
no more than wearing a scarf, or a hat,

00:16:08.890 --> 00:16:10.940
or a mask when you're trick or treating

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:12.290
would be child abuse.

00:16:12.290 --> 00:16:15.010
And if we're talking about
the message that it's sending,

00:16:15.010 --> 00:16:17.740
are we saying that the
entire continent of Asia

00:16:17.740 --> 00:16:18.940
is committing child abuse

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:22.190
when people are wearing masks
even in non-pandemic times?

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:25.470
Or that maybe since it doesn't
actually harm the people

00:16:25.470 --> 00:16:26.430
that are wearing masks,

00:16:26.430 --> 00:16:28.000
they wanna send a message.

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:28.833
At the end of the day,

00:16:28.833 --> 00:16:30.950
it's a decision that doesn't harm anyone

00:16:30.950 --> 00:16:32.000
including the children,

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:34.270
and it's a decision
that's up to the parents.

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:35.103
I don't know, man.

00:16:35.103 --> 00:16:36.570
It seems like after this
whole pandemic thing,

00:16:36.570 --> 00:16:38.610
we should be bending over
backwards to help parents

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:41.290
rather than calling the cops on them.

00:16:41.290 --> 00:16:42.690
At the end of the day,

00:16:42.690 --> 00:16:46.059
I guess even if you did
make a Tucker report,

00:16:46.059 --> 00:16:48.670
you'd have a hard time making
out a criminal or civil case

00:16:48.670 --> 00:16:51.240
but there's likely to
be a small subsection

00:16:51.240 --> 00:16:52.260
of Tucker watchers

00:16:52.260 --> 00:16:54.820
that if they follow
through with his advice,

00:16:54.820 --> 00:16:58.860
they might be subject to
criminal or civil penalties.

00:16:58.860 --> 00:17:01.330
And, I guess if there's one
thing that we can all agree on,

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:03.810
it's that you probably should never do

00:17:03.810 --> 00:17:06.080
what Tucker Carlson tells you to do.

